<title>UK: Northwest Europe oil, gas rigs down five to 62.</title>
<headline>Northwest Europe oil, gas rigs down five to 62.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of active oil and gas rigs in operation in offshore northwest European waters fell to 62 in the week to February 19 from 67 in the previous week, consultants Arthur Andersen said.</p>
<p>The number of active rigs in U.K. waters fell by two to 32 while Norway was unchanged at 19.</p>
<p>Danish drilling was also stable at three rigs while there were three fewer in Dutch waters, at eight rigs.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8167</p>
